        "raisedBy": [
          "accessibility"
        ],
        "recommendation": "Render the delete action as a native `<button type=\"button\" className=\"icon-button\" onClick={onDelete}>`. A keyboard user pressing Tab never lands on the div (no tabindex), and Enter or Space does nothing (no key handler), so they cannot delete a document — the change's only feature. A screen reader announces no button role either. WCAG 2.1.1 Keyboard, 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value. Keep the existing visual style and make sure the focus indicator stays visible (2.4.7).",
